1
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,920
Try stepping back and
looking at it in the light.

2
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:28,660
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,280
Walking while looking back,
my hand held by Mom.

4
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:42,340
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the tiles of the shopping arcade,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone forgets.

9
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,100
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:14,660
Go on, turn that corner.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there's a turtle there.

13
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town.

14
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:39,960
What happened?

16
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,100
Special exhibition

17
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:49,980
The Mona Lisa's big laugh...

18
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:51,460
We've been hit.

19
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:56,360
It's the Kamikaze Robber Dalc!

20
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,960
Here it comes! It's a shoujo manga, dega!

21
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,900
He's shown up again

22
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,140
Kamikaze Robber Dalc

23
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,240
That makes five this month.

24
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:10,420
Forget it, just leave it alone.

25
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:13,520
Anyway, it's none of our business.

26
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,600
He only goes after art pieces, after all.

27
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,160
Senpai! Ryo-san!

28
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:22,560
Idiot!

29
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,400
Chief! You're here?

30
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:31,600
Still wasting your time
playing with these things

31
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:35,180
The theft case has nothing to do with us,
you know.

32
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:37,000
How could it not have
anything to do with us?

33
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,180
It's just a light joke, a joke!

34
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:43,300
Well, lazing around playing
with these things ends today.

35
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:49,540
To solve this case, a specialist
has been dispatched from headquarters.

36
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:52,200
All of us will fall under his command.

37
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:55,440
We've had this pattern before, haven't we?

38
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:57,920
That pattern where a
pervert always shows up?

39
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,120
I bet another weirdo is coming.

40
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:03,480
Could it be that this specialist is

41
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,320
a detective from the Special
Investigations Division?

42
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:08,060
Well, yeah.

43
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:08,920
Just as I thought.

44
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:12,760
That guy from the detective
division over there,

45
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:15,040
none of them were normal, were they.

46
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:17,620
This time, it's fine.

47
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:20,420
I met him too,
and he was dressed perfectly ordinarily,

48
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:21,920
and his words and behavior were normal.

49
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:23,240
What's his name?

50
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,080
I didn't catch his name,

51
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,820
but he was called the "Profiling Detective."

52
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,360
Profiling Detective?

53
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,380
What's this "profiling" thing, anyway?

54
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:33,900
Allow me to explain.

55
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:38,000
Profiling is

56
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,980
deducing the culprit's
profile from tiny clues,

57
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:43,160
narrowing down the offender.

58
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,640
Take this tank,

59
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,980
which looks like an ordinary
model kit at first glance,

60
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:49,900
but it actually has reinforcements
hidden in subtle places.

61
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,460
This shows that the builder

62
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:53,900
was making model kits long
before Gunpla came out.

63
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,720
He's in his late thirties to forties.

64
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:02,040
The finish on each part is also
extremely delicate and meticulous.

65
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:03,760
But for this kind of work,

66
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,820
thick, burly fingers are
actually better suited.

67
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:09,820
And there's a faint manly odor.

68
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:12,400
Plus, he hasn't taken a bath in three days,
I'd say.

69
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,880
That means

70
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,520
he's most likely a single man.

71
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:19,420
Based on this information, my deduction is:

72
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,120
Here it comes.

73
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,660
It must be yours.

74
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:23,880
W-wow, that's amazing.

75
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,020
I got it right.

76
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,600
See? This is profiling!

77
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,040
So then, you...

78
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,300
Profiling, yeah, that's it.

79
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:34,920
Thank goodness,
he's pretty normal, isn't he?

80
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,660
No, we can't relax yet.

81
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:39,940
That's right, we've been burned
so many times by this pattern!

82
00:04:39,940 --> 00:04:41,660
We'd better be very careful.

83
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,520
Then let's begin the
investigation meeting right away.

84
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:49,420
The culprit has never once been seen.

85
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,420
But we have several leads to go on.

86
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:55,800
First, five illustrated
cards left at the crime scene

87
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:58,640
are written on letter
paper with drafting ink.

88
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:04,120
Furthermore, this part uses screentone S401.

89
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,080
Screentone?

90
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,380
Well, screentone is...

91
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:12,800
like patterned adhesive
sheets that manga artists use.

92
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:13,980
Exactly.

93
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:18,440
So we can deduce that the culprit
draws manga on a daily basis.

94
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:20,520
So the culprit is a manga artist?

95
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:24,900
Just because someone draws manga
doesn't make them a manga artist.

96
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:29,640
From what I can see, the culprit is a
woman aiming to become a shojo manga artist.

97
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:33,220
How can you be so sure of that?

98
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,740
This card

99
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,460
It has a faint smell of cosmetics.

100
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:42,240
There aren't many men who wear makeup and draw manga,
after all.

101
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:44,560
And above all, there's this name.

102
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,880
It's clearly a play on a
certain shojo manga title.

103
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:51,320
This shows the culprit
knows shojo manga well.

104
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:55,360
What's more, a pro wouldn't
plagiarize someone else's manga.

105
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,800
I see.

106
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,960
Probably.

107
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:03,920
Right, then let's focus the search on
women who aspire to be shojo manga artists.

108
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,360
Everyone, move out!

109
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:06,440
Yes, sir!

110
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:08,660
Hold on a second.

111
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:13,620
What is it?
Do you have something else to say?

112
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:18,320
Do you think profiling is
finished with just this much?

113
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:19,320
But now,

114
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:23,100
the real profiling begins.

115
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:28,280
Je t'aime, je t'aime, lollipop.

116
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:32,100
Why would a girl who wants
to be a shojo manga artist

117
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,260
What is this?

118
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,620
Have you ever heard the voice of the stars?

119
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:46,680
A voice whispering to you
from beyond the night sky.

120
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:50,600
It may be a message from that person to you.

121
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,580
See? I knew it would start.

122
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,020
Profiling Detective!

123
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:02,060
Asorica

124
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,700
Now, a splendid transformation!

125
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:08,640
I'm a girl who wants to
become a shojo manga artist.

126
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,580
Please call me Ruri-rin.

127
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:14,460
Where's the girl who wants to
become a shojo manga artist?

128
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:17,620
I never expected this pervert of a man...

129
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:18,560
How cruel!

130
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:22,660
Just because I'm ugly,
you didn't have to say that much.

131
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,880
That's not the point, damn it!

132
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,040
But that's okay.

133
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,060
Surely that one person will understand me.

134
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:31,980
The true face hidden beneath my glasses...

135
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:36,420
Eeeh!

136
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:37,540
That's not good enough!

137
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:41,260
You're supposed to say,
"You're cuter without your glasses!" right there,

138
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:42,960
as if I could say that!

139
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:43,760
Honestly!

140
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:47,260
You clearly don't understand
what shojo manga is all about.

141
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:48,560
*Huff*

142
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,220
Yeah, you all have to transform too.

143
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:53,180
What!?

144
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:55,600
Je t'aime, je t'aime, lollipop!

145
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:59,920
Everyone,
become shojo manga-hopeful girls together!

146
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:03,340
Yaah, what is this!

147
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:04,800
What the hell is this!

148
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:13,400
What is this supposed to be?

149
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:16,360
Why are we dressed like this too?

150
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:19,500
Well, to conduct profiling,

151
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:22,180
we have to understand the culprit's feelings,
you see.

152
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:24,100
Is dressing like this
going to help us understand?

153
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:27,240
The culprit's hobby this time is shojo manga,
darling.

154
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:30,160
So we have to immerse ourselves

155
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:32,380
completely in the world of shojo manga.

156
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,220
Where are Nakagawa and Reiko?

157
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,660
They haven't transformed at all, have they?

158
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:41,820
Those two can already pass in the
shojo manga world as they are, so

159
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:42,800
I see.

160
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,360
Don't get convinced!

161
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:47,340
Don't you think it's embarrassing
to be made to dress like this?

162
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,520
Hey, Chief.

163
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:54,520
But why are we dressed
as volleyball players?

164
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:58,220
Well, in shojo manga,

165
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:01,460
volleyball stories are the classic,
aren't they?

166
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:04,100
Are they?

167
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:07,040
Even Megumi Mizusawa-sensei writes them.

168
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:14,560
Then I'll thoroughly teach you about
the shojo manga world from now on.

169
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:18,580
In shojo manga,
creating atmosphere is what matters.

170
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:24,200
Let's blow away this stagnant air with
the shojo manga-style theme song I made!

171
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:28,140
Okay, music start!

172
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:42,700
Lu-lu-la-ra-lu-la-ra,
one step to the beat of spring,

173
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:48,120
I sprout wings and take flight, that's me!

174
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:59,820
No matter how painful things get,
even when tears are about to spill,

175
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:07,060
I won't lose,
because that special someone is here.

176
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:14,920
Lu-lu-lu-lu, fight!
Lu-ru-rin, fight! Lu-ru-rin!

177
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:20,760
I hear everyone calling my name, Lu-lu-love!

178
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:27,380
Yes, a smile is the ultimate energy!

179
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:30,145
See?

180
00:10:30,195 --> 00:10:34,200
Doesn't it feel like you're
starring in a shojo manga right now?

181
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:35,840
Yeah... right.

182
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:38,720
No, this isn't the shojo manga this time.

183
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,780
Then let's move on to the next step.

184
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:41,520
Yes.

185
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,480
No, absolutely not.

186
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,200
That's right, here we go.

187
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:48,800
Ange clo, ange clo.

188
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,960
Ashinami slide.

189
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,500
I never imagined I'd end up
going outside dressed like this.

190
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:01,980
Now, for the next step, everyone gets to
experience the shojo manga world firsthand.

191
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:03,200
How?

192
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:03,820
Don't worry.

193
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:09,420
Tutebu tutebu ralipo pink.

194
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:13,920
It'll become the perfect home for
a shojo manga heroine to live in.

195
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,780
What are they even doing?

196
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:24,040
It does feel a bit shojo, though.

197
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:28,880
Done!

198
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,740
So it was just a painted backdrop after all.

199
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:36,900
Don't worry about it.

200
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,960
But if we're shojo manga heroes,

201
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:43,420
shouldn't we have a more luxurious house?

202
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:44,460
Then

203
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:45,960
we could use my house.

204
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:48,680
We wouldn't have to travel far.

205
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,860
None of you understand anything.

206
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:52,600
Most of the readers are

207
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,340
ordinary girls, you know.

208
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,480
If we make the heroine that rich,

209
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,580
the readers won't be able to relate to her,
will they?

210
00:11:59,440 --> 00:11:59,760
I see.

211
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,760
Then next is the heroine's room!

212
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,500
Chu-teem, chu-teem, rally poppin!

213
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:09,460
Become the heroine's
room from a shojo manga!

214
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:16,520
This is going to take quite a while,
isn't it?

215
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:19,560
I'll stay calm too.

216
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,540
Excuse me, I'm going to step out.

217
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:25,360
Hey, that's cheating, Reikon!

218
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:27,480
Making all those excuses
and then running away!

219
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,920
Senpai, calm down!

220
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:39,140
Look how far we've come.

221
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:40,900
Everything's ready, so

222
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:44,620
now let me guide you into
the world of shojo manga.

223
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:49,620
This way.

224
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,700
This way.

225
00:12:56,780 --> 00:13:00,480
There are no more princes on white horses,

226
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,480
I've known that for a long time.

227
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,940
but I always believed a wonderful
meeting would come someday.

228
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:14,940
Ugh, no.

229
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:18,520
Mom, why didn't you wake me up?

230
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,680
I woke you up, many times.

231
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:23,880
I'll warm up some milk right away.

232
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,880
I don't need it, just this is enough.

233
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,700
Bye, I'm off!

234
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:30,160
Good grief, what an unimaginable thing.

235
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:33,860
I wish she'd act a bit more like a girl.

236
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:40,800
Are you all right?

237
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,920
That was how I met him.

238
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:53,900
What a perfectly shojo
manga-style scene this is!

239
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:54,760
How lovely!

240
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:58,040
Hey, what are we supposed to
do with this half-eaten bread?

241
00:13:58,460 --> 00:13:59,660
Don't worry about that kind of thing.

242
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:01,260
It's a shojo manga, after all.

243
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,060
I've been wondering
about this since earlier...

244
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:07,620
The shape of this car
seems pretty sloppy to me.

245
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:08,940
Don't look!

246
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:11,380
You know I'm bad at shojo manga makeup.

247
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:12,920
B-but...

248
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,260
And what's with these flowers anyway?

249
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:17,200
Where on earth are they coming from?

250
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,900
I don't really understand it, do I?

251
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:21,720
Shut up, shut up, shut up, shut up!

252
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:25,360
Then you should've just made a world without bread or cars,
shouldn't you?

253
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:32,460
Once upon a time,
there lived a princess named Jajauma.

254
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:37,160
Princess, princess,
where have you gone, Princess?

255
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:38,400
Princess!

256
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,800
Still not found?

257
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,140
Yes.

258
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:45,140
The princess's tomboyish
ways are truly a problem.

259
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:46,620
That one.

260
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,680
Princess, this is dangerous!

261
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,540
Please return, Princess!

262
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:54,700
Don't worry, old man.

263
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:57,900
I want to see how the common folk live!

264
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:07,900
Are you all right?

265
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:12,440
Y-you insolent wretch! Don't touch me!

266
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:15,040
What a spirited princess.

267
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:21,380
He was actually the young lord of a neighboring country,
who had come to this Wakasa village incognito.

268
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,500
This is how a romantic
period drama should be!

269
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:28,140
Hey, isn't this a little weird?

270
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:32,080
Normally there'd be a moat surrounding the castle,
wouldn't there?

271
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:37,420
Besides, if you're prowling around the castle with no reason to be there,
you'd definitely be suspected.

272
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,380
Don't worry about that.
It's a shojo manga, after all.

273
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:44,680
So what year and what region
is this story even set in?

274
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:49,860
If we don't know that, we can't set up
the costumes and backgrounds, you know.

275
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:52,480
Shut up!

276
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:55,300
Then, in that case,
let's go back to the basics here.

277
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,500
Let's make it a volleyball story.

278
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,800
Now, I'll announce the cast for
this performance's role of the back.

279
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:07,760
Heroine role: Ruriko Aso.

280
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:08,980
Yes.

281
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:13,540
for the leading man's role,

282
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,660
this connected-eyebrow guy, you're it.

283
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:17,760
What?

284
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:21,500
What's the answer?

285
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,160
What's wrong?

286
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,140
What do you mean?

287
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:24,300
No mistake about it.

288
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:25,900
I can't believe it.

289
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,300
Coach I can't do that.

290
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:31,300
I've only been doing ballet for a month.

291
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:33,940
Is that all you have to say?

292
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,260
Excuse me...

293
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:39,000
Rehearsal starts in ten minutes.

294
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:40,320
Don't be late.

295
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,040
Hurry, hurry!

296
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:51,120
If we're late,
Coach is going to chew us out.

297
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,880
There's a nail in my toe shoe!

298
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,360
Who on earth would do something like this?

299
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:01,100
Dad, yes, it must be Dad's doing!

300
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:04,440
So you think I stole Princess Rurika's leading man role,
don't you?

301
00:17:07,060 --> 00:17:08,820
What am I supposed to do?

302
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:10,240
Coach, please help me!

303
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,260
Coach!

304
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:12,920
How wonderful!

305
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:15,520
This is the very essence of shojo manga!

306
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,760
Hey, who exactly is this Otowa-san?

307
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:21,840
In shojo manga,
the villain has always been Otowa-san.

308
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:23,000
Well then, let's move on to the next one.

309
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,320
You still want to go on?

310
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,700
Enough already.

311
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:29,660
What are you saying?
The culprit still hasn't been caught!

312
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:30,660
Culprit?

313
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:33,460
Kamikaze Robber Dark, of course.

314
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,760
So you haven't forgotten about the case,
after all.

315
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:42,520
Until we arrest the culprit,
we can't stop studying shojo manga.

316
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:45,880
But at this rate, when will we ever...

317
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,900
That's right, a training camp!

318
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:49,980
A training camp?

319
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:53,680
Let's thoroughly study shojo
manga at a training camp.

320
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:57,660
Ryo-sama is going to a training camp?

321
00:17:57,980 --> 00:17:59,880
That's right, he left a week ago.

322
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,640
So, when is he expected to return?

323
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:05,560
Well, we can't get in touch with him.

324
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:25,560
Lu-la-la, lu-la-la, with one step in the summer breeze,
I'll become a mermaid and dive in, that's me!

325
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:37,380
No matter how sad things get, even
when my heart feels like it might break,

326
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:44,580
I won't give up,
because everyone is here with me.

327
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:46,980
La-la-la-la

328
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:52,460
Fight-lu-lilin, fight-lu-lilin

329
00:18:53,060 --> 00:18:57,180
I hear your voice calling me.

330
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:58,480
Ru-ru-ru

331
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:04,560
That's right, a smile is my greatest policy!

332
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:09,980
I... I'm getting dizzy...

333
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:12,740
R-Reiko-san?

334
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:16,060
Oh my! Maria, it's been ages,
you're looking so cute and bouncy!

335
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:17,860
Ryo-sama...

336
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:20,980
Coming through! I'll go bring the tea!

337
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:24,360
Hey, hey, Reiko!

338
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:26,940
Did anything happen while we were away?

339
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:28,860
Even Chief Ohara?

340
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,320
What's wrong with me?

341
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,340
What on earth is this...

342
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:36,260
Hehe, is it because of the training camp?

343
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:41,420
She's fully become a woman,
maybe even more than me.

344
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:43,860
What's wrong with Kei-chan?
What happened to Kei-chan?

345
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:45,160
Did you call?

346
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:49,700
Write "person" and "dream
" together, and you get "fleeting."

347
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:53,520
Man's dreams really are fleeting,
aren't they?

348
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,300
It's all right.

349
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:05,100
Until the day the flame of life burns out,

350
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:07,900
I'll keep chasing my dream.

351
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:08,520
Coach.

352
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:12,000
Even Kei-chan?

353
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,940
Let's all make the Coach's dream come true.

354
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:15,640
Yes.

355
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,100
Our dream is...

356
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:21,260
to catch the Kamikaze Robber
Darc who's shaking up the world

357
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:23,180
with our own hands.

358
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,360
Looks like you haven't forgotten about work.

359
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:29,340
Thanks to meticulous profiling,

360
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:32,300
I'm starting to understand
what the culprit is thinking.

361
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,040
Everyone, transform!

362
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:38,480
Je t'aime, je t'aime, knife hoppin'!

363
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,500
Become the Kamikaze Goat Darc!

364
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:47,820
What are you doing?

365
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:49,180
I'm changing clothes.

366
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:56,100
The Kamikaze Robber Darc has arrived!

367
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:00,700
Ryu-sama, what are you wearing?

368
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:04,680
The Kamikaze Robber Darc would
definitely be dressed like this.

369
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:07,140
I deduced it from the results of profiling!

370
00:21:07,460 --> 00:21:08,000
Hey!

371
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:11,540
Knowing only the crime isn't enough!

372
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:15,760
But you know, I also know where
the culprit will strike next!

373
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:16,640
Hey!

374
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,360
Really? That's amazing!

375
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:20,660
But...

376
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:25,080
It's written right here in the corner!

377
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:26,180
Whoa...

378
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:29,240
Shojo manga authors always do this,
don't they!

379
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:30,100
Hey!

380
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:32,280
Alright, everyone, let's go!

381
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:34,600
We're catching that guy tonight,
no matter what!

382
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,720
Everyone's a fighter!

383
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:45,560
Everyone, make sure you do your best.

384
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:50,620
I'll be watching over you all, always.

385
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:55,080
Nakagawa-san, are you all right?

386
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,860
Don't let yourself get carried away,
Maria-chan.

387
00:21:56,860 --> 00:21:58,500
It's acting, it's just acting.

388
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:03,120
I see, so you've been completely
steeped in shojo manga down to the bone.

389
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:06,640
Aim for the ace!

390
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:19,860
That's far enough!

391
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:22,560
The thief who's been terrorizing the public

392
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,700
won't get away with it!

393
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,740
The Kamikaze Robber Darc!

394
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:28,420
Today, she's going down for sure!

395
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,480
Damn it!

396
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:35,280
She's a man, just like us, isn't he?

397
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:38,880
Hey, didn't you say the culprit was a woman?

398
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:42,600
Even I can make a little
mistake now and then!

399
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,000
That's a big mistake!

400
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,680
What's the big deal? It's just this much!

401
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,280
You always do this, you know!

402
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:52,540
Forget that,
catching the culprit comes first!

403
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:54,800
Look, the culprit's running away!

404
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:55,580
There she is!

405
00:22:55,580 --> 00:22:56,540
Stop!

406
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,020
She's running this way!

407
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:00,100
Let go, let go!

408
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:14,520
Well, thanks to all of your cooperation,
we managed to make the arrest.

409
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:17,400
Tea time, everyone!

410
00:23:17,820 --> 00:23:18,660
Coming!

411
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:23,340
I'll be watching over you forever, you know.

412
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:27,280
I made mint tea today.
Wow, it smells lovely!

413
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:29,040
It's hot!

414
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:31,680
Well, what matters most is Mr. Sun,
after all!

415
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:32,460
This is...

416
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:33,501
Ever since that...

417
00:23:33,551 --> 00:23:37,340
it seems everyone can't come back
from the world of shojo manga.

418
00:23:38,100 --> 00:23:39,280
What are you going to do about it?

419
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:41,324
No,

420
00:23:41,374 --> 00:23:45,120
things like this happen quite often with this filing,
you see.

421
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:47,100
Put everyone back to normal!

422
00:23:47,340 --> 00:23:49,840
No, no, no, don't say that to me...

423
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:50,560
See ya!

424
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:53,220
Wait! Do something about it!

425
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:55,060
There's nothing I can do!

426
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:59,100
I'll be watching over you forever.

427
00:24:01,260 --> 00:24:05,620
Kicked the alarm clock,
stubbed my pinky, ouch-ouch-ouch.

428
00:24:07,420 --> 00:24:14,000
Quick eyebrows drawn,
then dash to the station, dash, dash, dash!

429
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:19,580
Packed on the train,
catching a nap with my back to the way home.

430
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:25,920
Another hard week,
so much overwork, all so very true.

431
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:30,600
Baguette in hand,
looking all cool and composed.

432
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:33,340
Beef bowl, large, extra sauce.

433
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:36,640
All the irritation from endless overtime,

434
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:40,280
let it out however you like.

435
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:46,420
Every day's no problem.

436
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:50,080
After a hot shower,

437
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:53,080
every day's no problem.

438
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:56,660
A sleep pillow restores my energy.

439
00:24:59,820 --> 00:25:02,580
Every day's no problem.

440
00:25:03,340 --> 00:25:06,240
I love myself just like this.

441
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,860
Every day's no problem.

442
00:25:08,860 --> 00:25:13,080
Monday, with hearts flying all around.

443
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,897
Hey!

444
00:25:18,947 --> 00:25:21,380
Ryotsu!

445
00:25:22,040 --> 00:25:24,660
What was it again?

446
00:25:24,660 --> 00:25:27,200
I had it just a moment ago, though.

447
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:29,320
Ah...

448
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:33,100
Right, that's it.

449
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:34,092
Next time,

450
00:25:34,142 --> 00:25:37,620
disaster strikes when you've forgotten,
so see you then, okay?

451
00:25:37,620 --> 00:25:40,660
That place has walls.

452
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,960
Well, I'm sure there are walls, too.

453
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:49,100
Everyone, come visit our town!

454
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,720
Thank you.

